What:           /sys/devices/.../ssc_service_count
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
Description:
                Read-only number of matching SSC service endpoints seen by a
                bound xiaomi,uke-ssc-iio platform controller. Zero means that no
                matching endpoint has been discovered. More than one prevents
                client admission; reading this attribute does not discover,
                contact or select a service.

What:           /sys/devices/.../ssc_lookup_fault
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
Description:
                Read-only 0/1 flag indicating that endpoint uniqueness could not
                be tracked. The existing transport refuses admission in this
                state. This attribute does not clear the fault.

What:           /sys/devices/.../ssc_suspended
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
Description:
                Read-only 0/1 flag indicating that SSC requests are paused by
                the existing suspend lifecycle. Reading does not resume the
                controller, issue QMI requests or enable a sensor.

What:           /sys/devices/.../ssc_client_connected
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
Description:
                Read-only 0/1 result of the existing transport admission:
                controller present and resumed, tracked unique endpoint, open
                client and matching discovery generation. This does not prove
                sensor discovery, valid metadata or calibrated sample delivery.

What:           /sys/devices/.../ssc_declared_sensors
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
Description:
                Read-only count of supported sensor datatypes declared in the
                controller's Device Tree, from 0 through 8. It does not identify
                fitted chips or establish physical sensor availability.

What:           /sys/devices/.../ssc_discovered_sensors
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
Description:
                Read-only count of declared sensors with an admitted SUID in
                the current client generation, from 0 through 8. Zero is
                reported when the client is not current. No SUID is exposed.

What:           /sys/devices/.../ssc_ready_sensors
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
Description:
                Read-only count of declared sensors with accepted metadata in
                the current client generation, from 0 through 8. Zero is
                reported when the client is not current. This does not report
                samples, calibration or physical accuracy.

What:           /sys/devices/.../ssc_registered_sensors
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
Description:
                Read-only count of declared sensors whose IIO devices have
                been registered, from 0 through 8. Registered devices may remain
                present after a service disappears, so this count alone does
                not prove that samples are available.

What:           /sys/devices/.../ssc_last_error
What:           /sys/devices/.../ssc_last_error_stage
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
Description:
                Read-only last negative errno and failure stage recorded during
                discovery in the current namespace generation. Stages are none,
                client, lookup, attributes or registration. Unknown stage values
                render as unknown. Success does not erase a previous failure;
                the existing generation invalidation resets the pair to 0/none.
                A failure from an older generation or after removal is ignored.
                These attributes do not retry requests or change admission.

                All controller attributes are installed by the driver core
                after successful probe and removed with driver teardown. Each
                read snapshots only status under the existing state lock.
                Separate files may reflect different snapshots. No client ID,
                SUID, sample, timestamp or calibration payload is exported.
